      "content": "That makes sense about the resilience. I'm particularly interested in those \"unexpected fluctuations\" you mentioned. When looking at the data for similar London junctions, we see these weird, non-linear spikes in delay that don't always align with simple volume increases or accidents. How would you model those types of irregular, high-friction interruptions in a flow simulation?",
